`context/instructions/diagram-mermaid.md` is the format contract for a diagram
written in **Mermaid**: a fenced `mermaid` block inside a Markdown document, so
the diagram stays diffable in git and readable by an agent without image
rendering. Read it together with `context/instructions/diagram.md` (the doctrine:
type, layout, honesty) and `context/instructions/development.md` (the process
contract).

## Nothing is dropped

The diagram is the document: a renderer draws it, it never rewrites it. A
diagram that only survives as a rendered image has lost its source, and every
edit has to start over.

## The block

A diagram is a fenced code block tagged `mermaid`, embedded in the document that
owns it. Every example under *One example per form* below is exactly such a
block, and that section is the module's one home for examples.

It is not a separate asset file: the diagram lives next to the prose it
explains, so the two move together. Authored SVG assets are a different lane
(`context/instructions/vector-svg.md`).

## Type keywords

Map the reader's question (see `diagram.md`) to a Mermaid keyword:

| Question | Keyword |
|---|---|
| steps and decisions over time | `flowchart` |
| messages exchanged in order | `sequenceDiagram` |
| states and transitions | `stateDiagram-v2` |
| data between stores and processes | `flowchart` with data-shaped nodes |
| entities and relations | `erDiagram` |
| parts and boundaries of a system | `flowchart` with subgraphs |
| a schedule over time | `gantt` |

## One example per form

Each row of the table above, written small: one construct per line, and the one
thing that form must not invent. Copy the shape, not the words — the labels come
from the source.

### steps and decisions over time — `flowchart`

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A[receive] --> B{in scope?}
  B -->|yes| C[process]
  B -->|no| D[refuse]
```

_Do not invent a branch, or an outcome of one, that the source does not name._

### messages exchanged in order — `sequenceDiagram`

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  Client->>API: POST /orders
  API->>DB: insert
  DB-->>API: id
  API-->>Client: 201 Created
```

_Do not invent a participant or a message the source does not name._

### states and transitions — `stateDiagram-v2`

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Draft
  Draft --> Active: publish
  Active --> Retired: retire
  Retired --> [*]
```

_Every transition carries its trigger, and neither exists unless the source
states it. `[*]` is the start and the end marker._

### data between stores and processes — `flowchart`, data-shaped nodes

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  C[client] --> P[service]
  P -->|write| S[(store)]
  S -->|read| P
```

_A store appears only if the source names one; a cylinder is not decoration._

### entities and relations — `erDiagram`

```mermaid
erDiagram
  AUTHOR ||--o{ DOCUMENT : writes
  DOCUMENT ||--|{ CLAIM : asserts
```

_A relation and its cardinality are a claim about the schema: take both from it._

### parts and boundaries of a system — `flowchart`, subgraphs

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph Edge
    A[client] --> B[gateway]
  end
  subgraph Core
    B --> C[service]
    C --> D[(store)]
  end
```

_A boundary is one the source draws; a `subgraph` around unrelated nodes invents
an architecture._

### a schedule over time — `gantt`

```mermaid
gantt
  dateFormat YYYY-MM-DD
  section Wave 1
  analysis :a1, 2026-11-01, 5d
  plan :a2, after a1, 3d
```

_Dates and durations are cited, never estimated; an invented start date makes the
chart a fiction with a timeline._

## Portable subset

Write the standard Mermaid the project's renderer draws. Prefer the plain
constructs — node shapes, arrows with short labels, a subgraph for a boundary —
over renderer-specific tweaks.

## Escaped characters

A label is not free text: some characters are syntax. A literal `|` is written
`#124;` — the pipe delimits an edge label — and a literal `#` is `#35;`. When a
label carries several of them, quote it instead: `A["themes | syllabi"]`. A
diagram that does not parse reaches the reader as raw text instead of a picture,
so the escaping is part of writing the block, not a defect to fix later.

## Anti-patterns

- Styling-only changes: a theme or colour tweak is not a diagram improvement.
- `classDef` sprawl: a class per node is a stylesheet, not a diagram.
- Relying on automatic layout: place by connection (`diagram.md`); never accept a
  default that scrambles the reading order.
- Beautifying the renderer: a prettier theme does not add information.

## Label semantics

A relationship label carries meaning (action, protocol, direction, async,
cross-boundary). Keep it short; never delete it to make room.

## Where a diagram lives

The four homes are stated once, in `diagram.md` (*Where the picture lives*); this
module owns the fenced-block form. Every diagram keeps its source block, and a
canonical export strips presentation-only marks.

## Boundary

- Doctrine (type, layout, honesty) defers to `context/instructions/diagram.md`.
- Authored SVG assets defer to `context/instructions/vector-svg.md`.
- Tool choice, install and code defer to
  `context/instructions/development.md`.
- This module names no rendering tool and no exporter.
